  "name": "h1-hound-facetank",
  "description": "ATTACK (CP2 houndframe): is the charge tell irrelevant to a player who refuses to react to it? This is the p4 traversal policy (hold right + mash Space, which is known to clear the base slice 3/3) plus held fire, run against ?hound=1 \u2014 so it traverses normally but never reads a plant, never leaves a lane, and never reroutes. Hound contact is ordinary contact damage and the player carries 3 hp behind CONFIG.player.iframesMs 1200, so a charge that lands inside an i-frame window is free. If this clears the fixture, the designed counterplay (read the plant, leave the lane, or bait the tumble) is optional and the tell is decoration. NOTE: the first version of this script held right and fire with NO jump, which cannot traverse the column-39 step at all - it jammed there 3/3 and never reached the hound. That run tested nothing about the hound and was replaced by this one; the jam itself is finding F8, and its negative crush margins re-confirm the wall-grind defect on this fixture.",
